Package: Rsassy
Title: R Bindings to the 'sassy' Approximate String Matcher
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sassy", "Contributors", email = "maintainer@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Rick", "Beeloo", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("Ragnar", "Groot Koerkamp", role = c("ctb", "cph"))
  )
Description: Provides R bindings to the 'sassy' Rust crate for fast approximate string matching over ASCII, DNA, and IUPAC sequences. The package uses R's native C API as the boundary so raw-vector and future 'ALTREP' access can be handled explicitly.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.91.0, xz
Suggests:
    tinytest
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
